        <body>
            <div xml:id="d672">

                <pb facs="0550" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg468"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1619.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-04-29"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 29, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 509.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise the Department
                    that a serious condition in the town of Parral, Chihuahua, was called to the
                    attention of the embassy by the consul at Saltillo, by the British legation
                    here, and by Mr. David B. Gemmill, of the West Mexican Mines (Ltd.),
                    recently.</p>
                <pb facs="0551" n="469" xml:id="pg469"/>
                <p>The situation seemed sufficiently serious to warrant the embassy in taking
                    immediate action, and I have the honor to inclose to the Department herewith
                    copies of two notes which I have addressed to the foreign office asking that
                    prompt and adequate protection be afforded the American lives and property in
                    danger.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>



